Also note: main.c has a typo on line 51: `ptread_create` → `pthread_create`.

User: we need to shorten ph_take_forks by 1 line, as the maximum length of a function can be 25 lines between first { and last }. i am not allowed ternary operators.

GitHub Copilot: The cleanest single fix: set `first`/`second` to the odd-case defaults unconditionally, then use a single `if` (no `else`) to override for even. This removes the `else { }` block — 3 lines gone, 2 added, net **-1**. Total goes from 26 to 25.

```c
void	ph_take_forks(t_philo *p)
{
	t_fork	*first;
	t_fork	*second;

	if (p->dinner->philo_count == 1)
	{
		pthread_mutex_lock(p->left);
		ph_print(p, "has taken a fork");
		return ;
	}
	first = p->right;
	second = p->left;
	if (p->id % 2 == 0)
	{
		first = p->left;
		second = p->right;
	}
	pthread_mutex_lock(first);
	ph_print(p, "has taken a fork");
	pthread_mutex_lock(second);
	ph_print(p, "has taken a fork");
	pthread_mutex_lock(&p->dinner->meal_lock);
	p->last_meal = ph_get_time_us();
	pthread_mutex_unlock(&p->dinner->meal_lock);
}
```

